 "verdict": "ESCAPE DESTINATIONS (arm 1), registered in experiments/prereg_escape_rival.json (sha256 cf1e02ff90ad..., frozen before any destination was decoded). ZERO forward passes: the values were already stored as argmax_ids. Sources are the 3471 shared probe strings; destinations are compared as DECODED STRINGS, never ids, per the F166 inversion.  KB: the largest single-destination share in any model is 33.2%, below the registered 0.5, so the raw figure is primary.  DECISIVE PAIR pythia-410m vs -deduped: agreement 0.6355 over 3462 shared escaping sources (raw 0.6355, modal-excluded 0.6418 over 2303).  SHOULD BE FAR: vs mamba-370m-hf 0.3493; vs rwkv-4-430m-pile 0.3393; vs gpt-neo-125m 0.3902.  PRECISION FLOOR (fp32 vs bf16, same weights): 0.7127 over 3463 sources.  KC, AND FOR THIS ARM THE NULL IS THE TEST: the decisive pair's observed agreement 0.6355 against a frequency-matched null of 0.1429 (sd 0.0056, p95 0.1514), observed percentile 100.0.  KC does not fire: the agreement survives frequency matching.  RESOLUTION AGAINST THAT FLOOR, derived: the decisive pair disagrees 1.27x as often as bfloat16 rounding of the same weights, against 2.26x (mamba-370m-hf), 2.3x (rwkv-4-430m-pile), 2.12x (gpt-neo-125m). So this estimand DOES resolve below family, modestly, where the self-continuation set of F183 gave a floor of exactly zero and could not.  AND A SECOND NULL THE PREREG DID NOT REGISTER, because KE says the base rate is what must be beaten here: if each model drew independently from its own escape distribution the decisive pair would agree 0.0798 of the time, against an observed 0.6355. Unregistered and descriptive.  KD: agreement correlates with destination diversity at r = -0.0932 across 66 pairs, below the registered 0.7.  IDENTIFICATION: rank-1 nearest neighbour by agreement puts 10 of 12 models beside their own family, 83% against a family-level chance of 22.7% and a majority-class rate of 42%; tie-aware 83%. FAMILY ATTRIBUTION, never instance identification.  REFUSALS, registered before the numbers: no p-value on the cohort (the null percentiles are within-comparison controls); no semantic reading of any token list; no cross-model comparison keyed on token id; no adjustment of any gate after the fact; no mechanistic claim. THE PRIOR-ART RE-CHECK OWED SINCE F183 IS STILL OWED and still blocks write-up.",
